.
.TH FFFM "1" "January 2019" "fffm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fffm \- :file_folder: A simple file manager written in bash
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fffm
.SH DESCRIPTION
A simple file manager written in bash.
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.
.nf

j: scroll down
k: scroll up
h: go to parent dir
l: go to child dir

enter: go to child dir
backspace: go to parent dir

\-: Go to previous dir\.

g: go to top
G: go to bottom

:: go to a directory by typing.

\.: toggle hidden files
/: search
t: go to trash
~: go to home
e: refresh current dir
!: open shell in current dir

x: view file/dir attributes
i: display image with w3m-img

down:  scroll down
up:    scroll up
left:  go to parent dir
right: go to child dir

f: new file
n: new dir
r: rename
X: toggle executable

y: mark copy
m: mark move
d: mark trash (~/.local/share/fffm/trash/)
s: mark symbolic link
b: mark bulk rename

Y: mark all for copy
M: mark all for move
D: mark all for trash (~/.local/share/fffm/trash/)
S: mark all for symbolic link
B: mark all for bulk rename

p: paste/move/delete/bulk_rename
c: clear file selections

[1-9]: favourites/bookmarks (see customization)

q: exit with 'cd' (if enabled).
Ctrl+C: exit without 'cd'.
.
.fi
.
.SH "Customization"
.
.nf

# Use LS_COLORS to color fffm.
# (On by default if available)
# (Ignores FFFM_COL1)
export FFFM_LS_COLORS=1

# Show/Hide hidden files on open.
# (On by default)
export FFFM_HIDDEN=0

# Directory color [0\-9]
export FFFM_COL1=2

# Status background color [0\-9]
export FFFM_COL2=7

# Selection color [0\-9] (copied/moved files)
export FFFM_COL3=6

# Cursor color [0\-9]
export FFFM_COL4=1

# Status foreground color [0\-9]
export FFFM_COL5=0

# Text Editor
export EDITOR="vim"

# File Opener
export FFFM_OPENER="xdg\-open"

# Enable or disable CD on exit.
# Default: '1'
export FFFM_CD_ON_EXIT=1

# CD on exit helper file
# Default: '${XDG_CACHE_HOME}/fffm/fffm.d'
#          If not using XDG, '${HOME}/.cache/fffm/fffm.d' is used.
export FFFM_CD_FILE=~/.fffm_d

# Trash Directory
# Default: '${XDG_DATA_HOME}/fffm/trash'
#          If not using XDG, '${XDG_DATA_HOME}/fffm/trash' is used.
export FFFM_TRASH=~/.local/share/fffm/trash

# Trash Command
# Default: 'mv'
#          Define a custom program to use to trash files.
#          The program will be passed the list of selected files
#          and directories.
export FFFM_TRASH_CMD="mv"

# Favourites (Bookmarks) (keys 1-9) (dir or file)
export FFFM_FAV1=~/projects
export FFFM_FAV2=~/.bashrc
export FFFM_FAV3=~/Pictures/Wallpapers/
export FFFM_FAV4=/usr/share
export FFFM_FAV5=/
export FFFM_FAV6=
export FFFM_FAV7=
export FFFM_FAV8=
export FFFM_FAV9=

# w3m-img offsets.
export FFFM_W3M_XOFFSET=0
export FFFM_W3M_YOFFSET=0

# File format.
# Customize the item string.
# Format ('%f' is the current file): "str%fstr"
# Example (Add a tab before files): FFFM_FILE_FORMAT="\t%f"
export FFFM_FILE_FORMAT="%f"

# Mark format.
# Customize the marked item string.
# Format ('%f' is the current file): "str%fstr"
# Example (Add a ' >' before files): FFFM_MARK_FORMAT="> %f"
export FFFM_MARK_FORMAT=" %f*"
.
.fi
.
.SH "Keybindings"
.
.nf
For more information see:
    https://github.com/dylanaraps/fff#customizing-the-keybindings

### Moving around.

# Go to child directory.
export FFFM_KEY_CHILD1="l"
export FFFM_KEY_CHILD2=$'\e[C' # Right Arrow
export FFFM_KEY_CHILD3=""      # Enter / Return

# Go to parent directory.
export FFFM_KEY_PARENT1="h"
export FFFM_KEY_PARENT2=$'\e[D' # Left Arrow
export FFFM_KEY_PARENT3=$'\177' # Backspace
export FFFM_KEY_PARENT4=$'\\b'   # Backspace (Older terminals)

# Go to previous directory.
export FFFM_KEY_PREVIOUS="-"

# Search.
export FFFM_KEY_SEARCH="/"

# Spawn a shell.
export FFFM_KEY_SHELL="!"

# Scroll down.
export FFFM_KEY_SCROLL_DOWN1="j"
export FFFM_KEY_SCROLL_DOWN2=$'\e[B' # Down Arrow

# Scroll up.
export FFFM_KEY_SCROLL_UP1="k"
export FFFM_KEY_SCROLL_UP2=$'\e[A'   # Up Arrow

# Go to top and bottom.
export FFFM_KEY_TO_TOP="g"
export FFFM_KEY_TO_BOTTOM="G"

# Go to dirs.
export FFFM_KEY_GO_DIR=":"
export FFFM_KEY_GO_HOME="~"
export FFFM_KEY_GO_TRASH="t"

### File operations.

export FFFM_KEY_YANK="y"
export FFFM_KEY_MOVE="m"
export FFFM_KEY_TRASH="d"
export FFFM_KEY_LINK="s"
export FFFM_KEY_BULK_RENAME="b"

export FFFM_KEY_YANK_ALL="Y"
export FFFM_KEY_MOVE_ALL="M"
export FFFM_KEY_TRASH_ALL="D"
export FFFM_KEY_LINK_ALL="S"
export FFFM_KEY_BULK_RENAME_ALL="B"

export FFFM_KEY_PASTE="p"
export FFFM_KEY_CLEAR="c"

export FFFM_KEY_RENAME="r"
export FFFM_KEY_MKDIR="n"
export FFFM_KEY_MKFILE="f"

### Miscellaneous

# Show file attributes.
export FFFM_KEY_ATTRIBUTES="x"

# Toggle executable flag.
export FFFM_KEY_EXECUTABLE="X"

# Toggle hidden files.
export FFFM_KEY_HIDDEN="."

.
.fi

.SH "Disabling keybindings"
.
.nf

You can't unset keybindings by making their value `''`.
What you need to do is change their value to `off`.

Example:

# KEY_GO_TRASH was bound to 't', now its unset.
export FFFM_KEY_GO_TRASH="off"

# KEY_MKFILE is now set to 't' and its original
# keybinding is also unset 'f'.
export FFFM_KEY_MKFILE="t"
.
.fi

.SH "Dealing with conflicting keybindings"
.
.nf

When rebinding a key in `fffm` make sure you don't have two bindings
with the same value. You can avoid this by setting the other
conflicting key-binding to something else or by changing its value to `off`.

.
.fi
